# Map Layout — No Incorrect Overlaps

When adding or moving world objects (zones, unlock pads, fields, buildings, trucks, NPCs, decor, fences), keep footprints clear of each other.

## Checklist before finishing a layout change

1. List new/changed positions with approximate half-extents (x, z).
2. Check AABB overlap against nearby fixed objects (fields, shop zones, DUMP/PROCESS/EGGS, pads, barn/coop, truck load/wait, fence).
3. Fix any **incorrect** stack (pad inside building, truck on field, zone on another zone, decor through fence, customers through solid fence).

## Allowed adjacencies (do not “fix”)

- PROCESS zone next to processor mesh
- Truck LOAD zone next to that bay’s wait/park pose
- Counter next to its SELL pad

## Typical footprints (approx half-size)

| Object | Half W×D |
|--------|----------|
| Unlock pad | 0.9 × 0.9 |
| Zone plane 1.6–2.2 | ~0.8–1.1 |
| Barn | 2.0 × 1.6 |
| Coop | 1.2 × 0.9 |
| Processor | 1.1 × 0.7 |
| Truck LOAD pad | ~1.1 × 1.0 (east border, inside fence) |
| Truck (parked) | ~0.75 × 1.65 (east fence gap) |
| Factory | ~1.6 × 1.2 |
| Conveyor belt | ~0.7 × 7+ |
| Train (parked) | ~0.75 × 2.5 (along N–S) |
| Train depot | ~2.1 × 1.6 |
| Portal gate | ~1.1 × 0.2 |
| Field1 | 4.2 × 2.4 |
| Field2 (wheat) | 3.2 × 1.8 |

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — unlock pad on field / truck wait on wheat
createUnlockPad('field2', …, new THREE.Vector3(12, 0, -3.5), …)
// waitPos lands inside field2

// ✅ GOOD — pad and waits clear of soil AABB
createUnlockPad('field2', …, new THREE.Vector3(15.8, 0, 5.0), …)
// truck wait z north of field2 north edge
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — egg zone inside coop footprint
eggPos = (7.5, -8.2); coop at (7.5, -8.2)

// ✅ GOOD — eggs in front of coop, chickens beside not inside
eggPos = (7.5, -6.0); coop at (7.5, -8.5)
```

After layout edits: mentally (or with a quick AABB check) verify pads vs buildings/fields/trucks/fence gates. If map expands, ensure shop2 has a real fence gate — not only a label on solid fence.
